Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the SAME reconciliation the DiskForecast
sibling log recorded.

NOTE: a prior parallel run logged a different-slot attempt under `TeslaSync/feature-views/`
with NO nav wiring (artifact-…-0497-SchemaDriftPage.log). That convention is NOT followed
here: this slot's built admin pages (DiskForecast et al.) use `Sources/Features/Admin/` +
real AppRoute/RouteHostRegistry nav wiring, and the directly-analogous DiskForecast page
(same 32-item shape, same admin-observability source) is the template followed.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the admin sub-path `/admin/schema-drift`. `.admin` is held
by the sibling DiskForecast page (the parser keys on the first path segment), so — exactly
as the LiveSignalInspector and FleetTelemetryCoverage siblings did for their admin
sub-paths — SchemaDrift gets a dedicated `.schemaDrift` AppRoute case plus an
`AppRouteParser` alias `/admin/schema-drift → .schemaDrift`. `SchemaDriftRouteRegistration`
hosts the page on that route; it is composed into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift, so
the page is reachable via the System-group sidebar entry and any `/admin/schema-drift`
deep link, without displacing DiskForecast.

