================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SchemaDriftPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/
success plus the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable SchemaDriftDataSource
seam whose value types mirror the Go/KMP SchemaDriftResult + schemacheck.{Drift,Fingerprint}
1:1 (production binds OperatorConfidenceStore.schemaDrift() through the seam). The page
reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the
drift-summary GlassPanel (status badge with AlertTriangle/CheckCircle2 semantics + three
count-delta stat cards, each with its "{current} current · {expected} expected" sublabel),
the fingerprints GlassPanel (current + expected fingerprint cards, each with the SHA-256 and
the Tables/Columns/Indexes count stats + the seed capture time), and the no-fingerprint
EmptyState — all on the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). A new
`.schemaDrift` route + parser alias + registration wire it into the shell navigation. Every
visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (22 keys; 21 added
+ admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle reused); display formatting (fmtNumber/formatDelta/
formatDateTime) is ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6
strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed model harness (30/30). The full
xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to one pre-existing, out-of-scope feature-views error
